---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { aggregates } from "../lib/data.js";
---

<Base title="About">
  <article class="session-head">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>A ledger, not a library.</h1>
    <p>
      In 1983 Apple gathered its developers at the Dunfey Hotel in San Mateo —
      the conference that became WWDC. This site keeps the modern record: every
      session Apple still publishes, indexed by category, duration, the code
      shown on screen, and how each session links to the others.
    </p>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="the-house">
      <h2 class="kicker" id="the-house">The house</h2>
      <figure class="house-figure">
        <img
          src="/about/dunfey-hotel-san-mateo-1985.webp"
          alt="The Dunfey Hotel in San Mateo, photographed in 1985 — a low building in the style of a Tudor castle."
          width="418"
          height="277"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="meta">The Dunfey Hotel, San Mateo, 1985.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        It opened as a Royal Coach Inn, built like a Tudor castle, and spent its
        years inside the Dunfey family's chain of motor inns before becoming the
        Regency Plaza in 1997. The site is a Marriott today.
      </p>
      <p>
        Its one claim on this page: in August 1983 it hosted the Apple
        Independent Software Developers Conference — the gathering that grew into
        WWDC. The trade report at the time ran under the headline
        <em>“Report from the Castle.”</em> We kept the name, and the date.
      </p>
      <p class="meta">
        Photograph and history from
        <a href="https://apple.fandom.com/wiki/Dunfey_Hotels" rel="external">Dunfey
        Hotels</a> on the Apple Wiki (Fandom), under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" rel="external license">CC&nbsp;BY-SA&nbsp;3.0</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
    <p>
      <strong>Everything links to the source.</strong> Videos, transcripts,
      sample code and documentation live at
      <a href="https://developer.apple.com">developer.apple.com</a>; this site
      stores metadata and aggregates only, for research and education,
      non-commercially.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Counted honestly.</strong> Apple revises its catalog over time —
      sessions are removed, labs are pruned, history shifts. Counts here come
      from snapshot {aggregates.snapshotId} of Apple's public feed (updated
      {aggregates.snapshotUpdated.slice(0, 10)}), and years before 2019 reflect
      what remains published, not the full conference that took place.
    </p>
    <p>
      Built as an open static site:
      <a href="https://github.com/elkraneo/dunfeyhotel.com">source on GitHub</a>
      (MIT). The data is fetched from Apple's public feed at build time and
      never committed.
    </p>
    <p class="meta">
      WWDC is a trademark of Apple Inc. This site is independent — not
      affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Apple. Analytics are
      self-hosted and cookieless; no personal data is collected. Questions or
      concerns: <a href="mailto:dunfeyhotel@reality2713.com">dunfeyhotel@reality2713.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .house-figure {
    margin: 1.2rem 0 1.4rem;
    max-width: 26rem;
  }

  .house-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-s);
    /* The period sepia of the session thumbnails suits a 1985 photograph. */
    filter: var(--thumb-filter);
  }

  .house-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
